{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.Su2Basis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.Su2Basis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Invertible.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.Basic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2KillingForm.orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2KillingForm.orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Orthogonality: ⟨eₐ, e_b⟩ = 0 for a ≠ b. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2KillingForm.normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2KillingForm.normalised","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L71-L71","doc":"Normalisation: ⟨eₐ, eₐ⟩ = -1/2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2KillingForm.killing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2KillingForm.killing","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L69-L69","doc":"The Killing form. Codomain a generic commutative ring in which `2`\nis invertible: the 𝔰𝔲(2) Killing form is q-independent, and its\nnormalisation `-1/2` is not an element of `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` but\nneeds nothing beyond `⅟2` (so `ℚ` is one instance, not the\nrequirement). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2KillingForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2KillingForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2KillingForm.toSu2Basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2KillingForm.toSu2Basis","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L62-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2KillingForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2KillingForm","kind":"structure","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L59-L73","doc":"The Killing form is negative definite on 𝔰𝔲(2):\n⟨eₐ, eₐ⟩ = −½ for the standard normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2Basis.comm_31","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2Basis.comm_31","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L57-L57","doc":"[e₃, e₁] = e₂. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2Basis.comm_23","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2Basis.comm_23","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L55-L55","doc":"[e₂, e₃] = e₁. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2Basis.comm_12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2Basis.comm_12","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L53-L53","doc":"[e₁, e₂] = e₃. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2Basis.bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2Basis.bracket","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The Lie bracket operation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2Basis.basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2Basis.basis","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The three basis vectors eₐ for a = 1, 2, 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2Basis.LieAlg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2Basis.LieAlg","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The Lie algebra carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2Basis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2Basis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Su2Basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Su2Basis","kind":"structure","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L42-L57","doc":"**𝔰𝔲(2) basis data**: three generators e₁, e₂, e₃ with\nstructure constants given by the Levi-Civita symbol. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantu